===================== BUGS FOUND + FIXED (via the real Xcode compile) =====================
  1. AppSettingsView.panel(_:_:) passed a NON-escaping @ViewBuilder closure into an
     escaping component closure — invisible to `swiftc -typecheck`, a hard error in
     full compile (and in the deferred xcodebuild). Marked `@escaping`. (mine)
  2. TeslaSyncShortcuts phrases were authored as key-strings
     ("intent.phrase.x.1 \(.applicationName)"). AppShortcutPhrase treats the literal
     as the SPOKEN phrase, so Siri would have matched the raw key. Rewritten as real
     natural-language phrases. (mine)
  3. Sources/App/RouteHostRegistry.swift (PRE-EXISTING P4/P4 b414508d) had a Swift-6
     `static let defaultValue = AppRouteHostRegistry()` non-Sendable global error —
     the navigation infra my Settings route-registration directly extends. Applied the
     canonical minimal fix `nonisolated(unsafe) static let defaultValue` (the default
     is an immutable empty registry). Tightly coupled to this prompt's change; the rest
     of the Shared-free app is strict-concurrency clean (proven: 53-file baseline = 0).

